#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hilbert_matrix

#% text
# `hilbert_matrix(n)` gives the n x n Hilbert matrix with entries 1/(i + j - 1).

#% text
# `hilbert_matrix([m, n])` gives the m x n one.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# See the usage above.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hilbert_matrix(3)
#% output
#= [[1, 1/2, 1/3], [1/2, 1/3, 1/4], [1/3, 1/4, 1/5]]

#% cell
hilbert_matrix([2, 3])
#% output
#= [[1, 1/2, 1/3], [1/2, 1/3, 1/4]]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Badly conditioned:

#% cell
det(hilbert_matrix(4))
#% output
#= 1/6048000

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `identity_matrix`, `det`
